# Factory ISO only (factory-iso/apply.sh). kmscon takes tty1 and runs the
# factory check there; getty keeps tty2. What keeps getty off tty1 is
# kmsconvt@.service's Conflicts=getty@%i.service, not this file: systemd's own
# package install enables getty@tty1 regardless, and the boot transaction drops
# its start job. Keep that line. If kmscon fails, OnFailure=getty@%i.service
# starts getty@tty1, whose drop-in autologs root into the same check (English
# only on that console).
# Two-token template form, as in 90-default.preset.
enable kmsconvt@.service tty1
enable getty@.service tty2
